======================================================================================
WHICH STORY
======================================================================================
  ungauged median D^2 is 1.28x the gauged median (21.85 vs 17.00)
  ungauged beyond training p99: 1.66%   gauged: 0.29%   expected under (a): ~1%
  ungauged AND FLAGGED beyond training p99: 8.82%

  STORY (a) -- METEOROLOGY. The ungauged cells sit inside the joint
  training distribution at close to the rate the training rows
  themselves do, so 13.16% is not the model extrapolating into a
  void. The P39 decision stands: score all 5,041, mark the 3,789.

  THE FLAGGED UNGAUGED CELLS ARE THE QUALIFICATION, AND THEY ARE PRINTED
  WHATEVER THE VERDICT SAYS. 8.82% of them sit beyond the training 99th
  percentile, against 1.33% of the flagged GAUGED cells -- 6.6x -- and their
  median D^2 of 44.73 is 2.5x the training median of 17.76. So the ALARMS
  raised outside the gauge grid are drawn disproportionately from the
  sparse edge of the training distribution, even though the ungauged
  field AS A WHOLE is not. That is a minority effect -- 91.2% of flagged
  ungauged cells are still inside the hull -- so it qualifies story (a)
  rather than replacing it with (b). Report it with the headline.

  IN-RANGE IS STILL NOT VERIFIED. This measures DISTANCE TO THE TRAINING
  DISTRIBUTION and nothing else. No gauge means no label ever existed
  there, so nothing at those points has been or can be scored. A cell
  can sit at the centre of the training cloud and still be wrong.

